WEBVTT

00:03.220 --> 00:08.070
Suggests they were attacked and tortured, 
but only up to the brink of death.

00:09.100 --> 00:11.560
They'll be alive,

00:11.560 --> 00:14.260
but they likely won't serve 
as a Saenome again.

00:15.210 --> 00:16.150
Damn it!

00:17.290 --> 00:20.490
The remnants of the puppets 
brought along as bodyguards.

00:20.490 --> 00:22.500
One's cut in two.

00:23.050 --> 00:25.040
One's burned to ash.

00:25.040 --> 00:26.920
One's shattered.

00:27.840 --> 00:31.260
There'll be at least three attackers,

00:31.610 --> 00:33.740
and a torture-happy bunch, at that.

00:35.040 --> 00:36.090
Can it be...

00:36.920 --> 00:41.020
It'll be the Sogenbi.

00:42.360 --> 00:45.020
Been a while since anyone 
picked a fight with us.

00:45.700 --> 00:48.810
Let's find them and crush them.

00:58.910 --> 01:06.670
<i>Malevolent Spirits</i>

02:19.990 --> 02:24.990
<b>Fire</b>

02:25.470 --> 02:27.180
Now, you be careful...

02:27.180 --> 02:30.250
You be <i>real</i> careful not to get hurt!

02:30.250 --> 02:34.750
I'm tired of you coming home 
covered in cuts and bruises.

02:34.750 --> 02:36.120
Y-Yes.

02:36.700 --> 02:39.010
I shall endeavor to be safe, Nagatsuki-s—

02:41.520 --> 02:42.230
B...

02:43.520 --> 02:44.640
Botan.

02:45.730 --> 02:46.640
Yep!

02:48.760 --> 02:49.710
Hostility?!

02:49.710 --> 02:50.570
Hey!

02:52.870 --> 02:56.110
No honorific? At least use "san"!

02:56.110 --> 02:57.370
But Naga—

02:58.060 --> 02:59.610
Botan told me to say that.

02:59.610 --> 03:00.860
Again?!

03:01.360 --> 03:02.670
It's no big deal.

03:02.670 --> 03:05.370
He doesn't use "san" with anyone else's name.

03:05.690 --> 03:09.750
Besides, it looks like 
that training's paid off!

03:12.040 --> 03:13.370
B... B...

03:13.370 --> 03:14.750
Bot... Bota...

03:14.750 --> 03:16.710
You're almost there! Push through!

03:19.400 --> 03:21.700
<i>Was it really worth pushing for?</i>

03:25.010 --> 03:27.560
I hope they'll be okay together.

03:28.110 --> 03:30.200
Don't you guys have to join them?

03:30.750 --> 03:33.690
Nah, we're on house duty today!

03:37.020 --> 03:38.430
Still...

03:38.430 --> 03:42.300
For them to ask for not just me, 
but the Nagatsuki household...

03:42.810 --> 03:45.030
The opponent must be impressively powerful.

03:45.030 --> 03:49.040
Yes, it's the Tsukumogami group 
known as "Sogenbi."

03:49.620 --> 03:52.040
One of the largest factions in Kyoto.

03:52.520 --> 03:54.200
Of particular note,

03:54.200 --> 03:57.420
their members' vessels are all implements of

03:57.420 --> 04:01.800
execution, torture, and other 
instruments of human suffering.

04:02.280 --> 04:07.540
Four years ago, the Kyoto Saenome 
went to war to take them down.

04:08.860 --> 04:14.090
This most recent incident must be the work 
of three of their surviving leaders.

04:15.190 --> 04:17.050
They sound quite dangerous.

04:20.540 --> 04:23.710
You're sure we shouldn't have 
brought Nagi and the others?

04:23.710 --> 04:28.080
Yeah. We were part of 
taking them down last time.

04:28.950 --> 04:31.830
If they're after revenge,

04:32.270 --> 04:35.900
they might attempt to 
take Botan as a hostage.

04:37.750 --> 04:41.930
Kushige, it might be best to expand 
the mansion's barrier a bit.

04:48.880 --> 04:49.880
I see.

04:50.470 --> 04:54.650
Or... are you <i>scared</i> without them?

04:54.650 --> 04:55.840
Don't be absurd.

04:56.780 --> 05:00.110
We're facing tsukumogami that harm humans.

05:00.960 --> 05:04.870
I'm relieved that I won't have to hold back.

05:08.370 --> 05:11.120
<b>Kazahana Park</b>

05:11.920 --> 05:14.630
This was the meeting place.

05:14.630 --> 05:17.040
Hyoma-chan!

05:19.700 --> 05:20.750
You—

05:21.440 --> 05:22.760
Identify yourself!

05:24.280 --> 05:25.760
How've you been?

05:26.580 --> 05:29.260
You're... Kadomori Tsubaki!

05:29.260 --> 05:31.050
Right-o!

05:31.050 --> 05:33.390
Looks like we're working together today!

05:34.640 --> 05:37.870
Anyway, how come you didn't text me?

05:37.870 --> 05:39.230
I waited, like, forever!

05:39.520 --> 05:41.300
I had my reasons—

05:45.740 --> 05:49.600
You've got a woman in every town, do you?

05:49.600 --> 05:52.080
I'll let Botan know.

05:52.080 --> 05:53.330
I do not!

05:54.610 --> 05:56.810
Sorry for messing with you like that.

05:57.360 --> 05:59.450
Nice to work with you today, Yu.

06:00.460 --> 06:02.000
You know each other?

06:02.000 --> 06:03.550
Of course we do.

06:03.550 --> 06:08.840
I'm more surprised to see 
how close <i>you</i> two are.

06:09.820 --> 06:14.510
Of course, Tsubaki's in the running to be 
the next Kyoto Saenome representative.

06:14.510 --> 06:19.000
It's in House Kunato's interest 
that you two should be so close.

06:19.000 --> 06:20.520
I wish you a happy life together!

06:20.810 --> 06:22.150
It's not like that!

06:22.150 --> 06:26.030
Incidentally, she and I mainly 
just grab coffee on occasion.

06:26.330 --> 06:29.260
Yu loves her coffee, right?

06:29.680 --> 06:31.030
Y-Yes...

06:31.720 --> 06:33.880
Where are the other Saenome?

06:33.880 --> 06:35.080
Nowhere.

06:35.540 --> 06:37.540
What you see is what you get.

06:37.950 --> 06:40.790
You guys are on your own mission.

06:41.150 --> 06:44.340
We'll be guiding you to your destination.

06:44.760 --> 06:47.690
And just FYI, the guiding's all you get.

06:47.690 --> 06:50.680
Don't expect us to join in the fighting.

06:50.680 --> 06:53.930
The informant... Aogi, wasn't it?

06:54.360 --> 06:56.030
Hey there, buddy.

06:56.030 --> 06:57.930
It's been a while.

06:57.930 --> 07:00.690
Why are we on our own mission?

07:00.690 --> 07:03.150
The rep and his main squad

07:03.530 --> 07:08.650
are at the place where shit went down, 
setting up a radar network of talismans.

07:09.180 --> 07:13.740
Once it's finished, they'll have all 
of Kyoto under their watchful eye.

07:14.660 --> 07:18.920
In the meantime, 
you'll be doing your own thing,

07:18.920 --> 07:22.370
sniffing out the shady little places 
they'd most likely be hiding.

07:23.010 --> 07:25.380
And that's something you'd know?

07:25.380 --> 07:28.100
Bingo! Give the man a prize!

07:30.290 --> 07:31.900
Their hideout...

07:32.510 --> 07:37.430
Not likely they're using it now that 
they've shown their hand, of course.

07:38.020 --> 07:42.020
Here's just hoping they left 
behind a clue of some kind.

07:42.490 --> 07:43.900
Wait a minute.

07:43.900 --> 07:46.520
You're telling me you 
<i>just</i> found their hideout?

07:47.040 --> 07:49.370
Aogi, you...

07:52.220 --> 07:53.510
You're incredible!

07:56.110 --> 07:57.820
Aogi, you've done well.

07:57.820 --> 07:59.160
Oh, w-well...

07:59.160 --> 08:02.350
Hyoma-chan doesn't know about connivance?

08:02.350 --> 08:04.790
He'd probably be angry if he found out.

08:05.230 --> 08:11.300
<i>Connivance... letting lawbreaking 
tsukumogami run free, if under supervision.</i>

08:12.050 --> 08:15.950
<i>Kadomori had granted connivance 
to the Sogenbi's remnants</i>

08:15.950 --> 08:19.180
<i>while using Aogi and Uchiki 
to check in on them periodically.</i>

08:19.180 --> 08:23.440
<i>It makes it easier to track the 
movements of the minor hooligans</i>

08:23.440 --> 08:25.130
<i>who come seeking their approval.</i>

08:25.840 --> 08:28.280
<i>"We let you roam free, 
and you don't turn on us."</i>

08:28.910 --> 08:31.560
<i>The Sogenbi would have 
known that was the deal.</i>

08:32.690 --> 08:35.670
<i>They've stayed quiet 
for years now, after all.</i>

08:36.370 --> 08:40.080
<i>Why would they break that unspoken law now?</i>

08:41.240 --> 08:46.200
<i>We've become quite the lawbreakers 
ourselves in their eyes, I suppose.</i>

08:46.880 --> 08:51.500
<i>You're becoming quite a point 
of contention, Kunato Hyoma.</i>

08:52.590 --> 08:55.590
A-Anyway, this is as far as I go.

08:55.590 --> 08:57.690
Let's blow this joint.

08:57.690 --> 09:00.440
We're not staying here 
any longer than we have to.

09:00.440 --> 09:02.220
C'mon, Uchiki-kun.

09:05.160 --> 09:05.940
Aogi!

09:05.940 --> 09:07.770
What now?

09:07.770 --> 09:09.190
Don't try to stop—

09:17.260 --> 09:18.370
They <i>are</i> here?!

09:21.720 --> 09:25.290
One... two... three.

09:25.640 --> 09:27.000
Well, well...

09:27.000 --> 09:29.290
Not many of you, are there?

09:29.290 --> 09:32.970
Aw, c'mon. There's a whole two of them!

09:32.970 --> 09:34.220
Three.

09:37.940 --> 09:39.660
Yes, I see...

09:39.660 --> 09:42.560
Kadomori Taiju put a watch on the town?

09:42.960 --> 09:44.960
What a pity...

09:44.960 --> 09:46.560
For you, that is.

09:46.560 --> 09:50.060
<b>— Hikikiri —</b>

09:46.970 --> 09:50.060
We didn't know the location 
of Kadomori's stronghold,

09:50.060 --> 09:52.220
so we'd decided to wait.

09:53.070 --> 09:55.130
That Saenome last night...

09:55.130 --> 09:57.070
He was a fine soldier.

09:57.610 --> 10:02.390
No matter how we tortured him, 
he wouldn't reveal his master's location.

10:05.020 --> 10:08.710
Let's see how much <i>you</i> can endure.

10:12.590 --> 10:14.710
<b>— Shimoto —</b>

10:16.970 --> 10:18.720
H-Hang on...

10:18.720 --> 10:22.570
How'd we end up surrounded?!

10:18.760 --> 10:20.590
<b>— Mushiro —</b>

10:26.920 --> 10:28.200
Sogenbi...

10:28.780 --> 10:31.850
For what purpose do you hurt humans?

10:33.270 --> 10:36.360
Did you attack that Saenome 
for the purpose of revenge?

10:36.810 --> 10:38.440
For what purpose?

10:38.860 --> 10:42.100
We do it to make humans suffer.

10:42.770 --> 10:47.140
That is naught but our fate, as those who take 
instruments of punishment as their vessel.

10:48.280 --> 10:49.420
I see.

10:50.330 --> 10:52.560
And when we attacked the Saenome,

10:52.560 --> 10:55.880
we were turning them from an 
obstacle to a target, nothing more.

10:56.420 --> 10:57.700
Did you...

10:58.240 --> 11:00.890
Yes, I see.

11:03.160 --> 11:04.550
I'll break you!

11:04.910 --> 11:08.120
I believe you see the Nagatsukis 
as obstacles, as well.

11:08.120 --> 11:10.560
It's in our interest to crush you now, then.

11:10.560 --> 11:13.710
Hyoma-chan happens to be right here.

11:13.710 --> 11:15.820
Guess I'd better put on a good show.

11:16.340 --> 11:18.220
Um, so...

11:19.810 --> 11:21.570
Uchiki-kun?

11:21.570 --> 11:24.570
This is not a good day.

11:25.160 --> 11:27.330
Tsukumogami Group, Sogenbi...

11:31.060 --> 11:32.660
Begone from this world!

11:39.880 --> 11:42.010
<i>The door pulls of the Kunato...</i>

11:42.010 --> 11:44.180
<i>So he's the one...</i>

11:45.010 --> 11:47.510
<i>Show me, Hyoma-chan.</i>

11:47.920 --> 11:51.690
<i>The strength that Hayato-san 
and Kusui-san boasted about.</i>

11:51.690 --> 11:54.470
<i>If you show me that here...</i>

11:54.900 --> 11:59.370
<i>I'll know for sure that you're 
the one I've been waiting for.</i>

12:00.800 --> 12:03.640
It's feeling like we're gonna 
get dragged into this fight.

12:03.640 --> 12:04.910
You gotta be kidding me!

12:07.400 --> 12:11.080
I'll have to pretend I'm 
helping out the Saenome,

12:11.080 --> 12:12.480
then slip away in the chaos!

12:12.480 --> 12:13.230
Okay...

12:13.230 --> 12:13.830
Here!

12:14.610 --> 12:16.840
Huh? Is that...

12:17.200 --> 12:18.840
A control talisman?!

12:18.840 --> 12:21.550
Have a good time, Aogi!

12:22.450 --> 12:24.970
H-Hey!

12:24.970 --> 12:26.800
You're pure evil!

12:31.930 --> 12:33.850
Time to make a break for it!

12:35.300 --> 12:35.940
Ow!

12:48.570 --> 12:49.430
Tsubaki!

12:52.710 --> 12:56.790
I'll face you myself.

13:07.550 --> 13:10.560
Couldn't you turn up the heat a bit?

13:13.040 --> 13:15.940
Nagatsuki, and Kunato...

13:16.320 --> 13:21.100
The human who broke the law by approaching 
the Nagatsukis, Kunato Hyoma...

13:22.210 --> 13:23.610
I am grateful to you.

13:24.400 --> 13:29.180
Your actions freed us from 
that ridiculous obligation

13:29.180 --> 13:32.450
and allowed us to act.

13:32.910 --> 13:34.580
I was the reason?

13:37.960 --> 13:41.290
Hyoma, now's not the time to think about—

13:44.840 --> 13:46.300
He's...

13:47.080 --> 13:49.550
I'll not be led astray by nonsense.

13:49.550 --> 13:51.810
Strike him quickly, Yu!

13:52.520 --> 13:55.680
Goodness. He is quite a fool.

13:57.400 --> 13:59.670
Kindly don't order me around.

14:09.320 --> 14:10.660
<b>Kadomori</b>

14:11.840 --> 14:13.880
Nothing but servants.

14:14.660 --> 14:16.780
Ume, Matsu...

14:16.780 --> 14:18.360
Leave them to me.

14:19.960 --> 14:22.010
Hang on a minute, Shimoto!

14:22.010 --> 14:23.960
We're friends, aren't we?

14:23.960 --> 14:27.240
Plus, we're just doing what 
the control talisman tells us to!

14:27.240 --> 14:28.720
We're really not here to fight!

14:29.040 --> 14:32.590
Huh? I've never liked you two, y'know.

14:32.590 --> 14:36.100
The way you scamper around, 
running your schemes...

14:37.710 --> 14:42.510
You know those Kadomori puppets 
we destroyed last night?

14:42.510 --> 14:46.990
You two are pretty much 
the same from our perspective.

14:47.410 --> 14:50.740
Did you call us puppets?

14:50.740 --> 14:53.990
You can't brown-nose your way out of this!

14:57.210 --> 14:59.290
Okay, damn it...

14:59.290 --> 15:01.710
That one really ticked me off.

15:02.350 --> 15:04.490
Let's do this, Uchiki-kun.

15:05.460 --> 15:08.600
I don't want to hear about pride...

15:08.600 --> 15:11.230
from a human bootlicker like you!

15:11.230 --> 15:14.930
That's rich, coming from someone 
humans granted connivance!

15:45.750 --> 15:47.220
<i>He self-detonated?</i>

15:47.640 --> 15:48.250
<i>No...</i>

15:56.090 --> 15:56.810
Hyoma!

16:01.620 --> 16:03.480
Your hairpins...

16:03.880 --> 16:07.440
They seal in place anything 
they hit. Quite dangerous.

16:08.310 --> 16:11.400
But our bodies are already an assumed form.

16:11.900 --> 16:17.240
If we instantly re-transform wherever 
they strike, it's not difficult to avoid them.

16:17.990 --> 16:20.600
Just stay quiet there for a while.

16:26.340 --> 16:28.380
Now for you.

16:28.930 --> 16:31.400
Your eyes have some life in them.

16:32.770 --> 16:37.300
<i>Anything that crosses the path of those 
"door pulls" is completely erased.</i>

16:38.050 --> 16:40.140
<i>The Kunatos' relic...</i>

16:40.140 --> 16:42.490
<i>The door pulls, "Chibiki-iwa"...</i>

16:42.830 --> 16:45.260
<i>So the rumors were true.</i>

16:47.110 --> 16:50.890
<i>The literal pulls from the door 
to the land of the dead.</i>

16:53.600 --> 16:55.360
<i>To come into contact with them</i>

16:55.360 --> 16:57.700
<i>is to step through that door.</i>

16:58.180 --> 17:00.220
<i>And that change in their natural law</i>

17:00.220 --> 17:03.000
<i>causes things of the world 
of the living to vanish.</i>

17:05.020 --> 17:06.850
Terrifying.

17:06.850 --> 17:08.080
However...

17:08.080 --> 17:10.840
The ability to use them comes 
down to the wielder's skill.

17:11.180 --> 17:14.840
And with your leg in that state, 
your mobility is halved.

17:15.360 --> 17:19.100
It's time to fulfill my purpose, then.

17:19.880 --> 17:23.350
I'll tear you to pieces, 
slowly and carefully.

17:25.560 --> 17:27.740
It's time for torture.

17:27.740 --> 17:29.650
Scream, cry...

17:50.590 --> 17:53.880
And then lose all hope.

18:00.680 --> 18:02.550
You can't back down, can you?

18:06.110 --> 18:07.390
Impossible...

18:07.920 --> 18:12.900
You can't afford to lose in a place like this, 
against an opponent like that...

18:13.210 --> 18:18.660
Because the thing you must destroy 
is far more powerful.

18:18.970 --> 18:21.660
Seeing you wield the door pulls they left you

18:21.930 --> 18:24.870
makes it clear that we're 
focused on the same thing.

18:25.300 --> 18:27.020
At last, we meet...

18:31.440 --> 18:33.960
The one who hunts the paper umbrella.

18:38.270 --> 18:40.970
Is that the best you have, Sogenbi?

18:41.720 --> 18:43.970
My compatriot.

18:49.370 --> 18:50.520
She's...

18:51.880 --> 18:54.360
Just because we're lower rank...

18:54.360 --> 18:56.230
You better not look away!

18:56.230 --> 18:57.340
You—

18:58.740 --> 19:01.610
So long, Shimoto-san!

19:09.000 --> 19:10.860
Nice work, m'dear!

19:10.860 --> 19:13.320
You've slimmed down a bit, I see.

19:13.320 --> 19:15.750
How many layers left, Uchiki-kun?

19:18.010 --> 19:20.760
We're down to the wire, I guess.

19:23.350 --> 19:26.120
Might be time to throw in the towel,

19:26.120 --> 19:27.770
Mr. Hikikiri.

19:32.260 --> 19:36.520
Implements of torture have a purpose.

19:39.500 --> 19:43.160
I learned through four 
years of stifling silence...

19:43.860 --> 19:48.600
Living, for us, means acting out our purpose!

19:48.600 --> 19:49.620
No freaking way...

19:49.620 --> 19:53.630
I won't stop! I won't stop! I won't stop!

19:55.590 --> 19:58.130
To achieve my purpose in life,

19:58.440 --> 20:00.280
you all must...

20:00.720 --> 20:02.260
die!

20:06.680 --> 20:09.060
Y-You...

20:14.880 --> 20:16.670
Is she mad?

20:16.670 --> 20:18.320
Oh, hey...

20:19.010 --> 20:20.570
The building is...

20:21.320 --> 20:23.070
N-No way...

20:24.450 --> 20:27.580
She bound up the whole building?!

20:27.580 --> 20:29.690
Now, there's something I didn't know.

20:29.690 --> 20:31.990
You get scary when you're mad, huh, Yu?

20:35.800 --> 20:38.090
<i>Get out of here. You're injured.</i>

20:40.400 --> 20:41.590
<i>Understood.</i>

20:45.470 --> 20:48.810
Get out of my way, Nagatsuki!

20:50.310 --> 20:53.600
Don't underestimate me!

20:53.600 --> 20:55.400
That's right!

20:55.710 --> 20:59.150
Learn the weight of the hammer of justice!

20:59.420 --> 21:00.650
What are you doing?!

21:00.960 --> 21:02.900
I'm following your plan, Yu!

21:02.900 --> 21:04.140
I didn't—

21:04.140 --> 21:06.700
F-Fine, do whatever you want!

21:05.910 --> 21:07.200
<b>Release</b>

21:14.200 --> 21:17.130
Kunato!

21:23.960 --> 21:25.930
What a dumbass.

21:33.070 --> 21:35.690
A magnificent collaboration!

21:39.190 --> 21:41.230
Why the hell did you do that?!

21:41.230 --> 21:42.300
But you said—

21:42.300 --> 21:43.360
I never said that!

21:43.360 --> 21:47.560
And didn't Botan tell you 
<i>not</i> to injure yourself?!

21:47.560 --> 21:49.150
She did, but—

21:49.150 --> 21:49.720
Stupid!

21:49.720 --> 21:50.450
B-But—

21:50.760 --> 21:52.020
Stupid!

21:52.020 --> 21:53.920
What's wrong with you?!

21:53.030 --> 21:54.950
Isn't that what you wanted?!

23:24.960 --> 23:39.980
<b>Next Time</b>

23:24.960 --> 23:39.980
<b>Radiance</b>
